  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multisectoral Support for Conflict-Affected Populations in Sudan and Abyei Northern PCA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The armed conflict in Sudan that erupted in April 2023 has led to the internal displacement of over 10.7 million people and affected millions more across the country as of September 2024, leading to a devastating humanitarian situation. Nearly twenty five million people (almost half of Sudan&apos;s population) require assistance, a 57 per cent increase from pre-conflict levels. Considering current health, water, sanitation and hygeine, non-food item and higher education needs related to the evolving conflict as well as the flooding and disease outbreak in Sudan, the International Organization for Migration seeks to respond holistically to the urgent needs of conflict-affected populations in North Darfur, Northern, Kassala, Gedaref, River Nile, Red Sea states and in Abyei North.</narrative>
  </description>
